  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0120 database is designed to store information about sports seasons, teams, and games. The database contains nine tables that work together to provide a comprehensive view of the data. The seasons table stores information about each season, including the season number, day zero date, and regional designations. The teams table holds information about each team, with a unique team ID and team name. The regular season compact results and detailed results tables store information about each game played during the regular season, including the season, day number, winning and losing teams, scores, and locations. The tourney compact results and detailed results tables store similar information for tournament games. The target table stores predictions and win-loss records for specific teams in a given season. The tourney seeds table stores information about the seeding of teams in the tournament, including the season, seed, and team ID. Finally, the tourney slots table stores information about the slots in the tournament, including the season, slot, strong seed, and weak seed. Each of these tables is linked to the teams table through foreign keys, which ensures data consistency and allows for efficient querying of related information. The database also enforces referential integrity through ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE rules, which automatically update or delete related data when a record is deleted or updated.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project is to develop a data-driven application for analyzing the 2015 NCAA Basketball Tournament. The system will manage and analyze tournament data, including regular season and tournament results, team performance metrics, seeds, and slots. The existing database schema supports the storage and retrieval of historical match data and predictive modeling information.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe main objective is to provide users with a comprehensive platform for accessing and analyzing NCAA tournament data. The system should enable detailed performance analysis and prediction of match outcomes based on historical data.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Sports Analysts: To analyze tournament data and derive insights.\n- Coaches and Team Managers: To understand team performance and opponent analysis.\n- Data Scientists: For predictive analytics and modeling match outcomes.\n- Basketball Enthusiasts: For accessing tournament data and statistics.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Management: \n   - Store and retrieve regular season and tournament data, including detailed match statistics such as scores, location, and number of overtimes.\n   - Manage team information and season data, including regions, seeds, and slots.\n\n2. Performance Analysis:\n   - Provide detailed statistical analysis of regular season and tournament matches.\n   - Allow comparison of team performance metrics and historical outcomes.\n\n3. Predictive Modeling:\n   - Enable prediction of match outcomes using historical data and predefined models.\n   - Store prediction results and evaluate prediction accuracy.\n\n4. User Interface:\n   - Develop an intuitive interface for data visualization and analysis.\n   - Provide tools for filtering and querying team and match data easily.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The system should efficiently handle large datasets and ensure quick query responses.\n- Scalability: Support scalability to accommodate future expansion of data and users.\n- Security: Ensure secure access to sensitive data and analytics features.\n- Reliability: Maintain high availability and reliability of data analysis and prediction services.\n- Usability: Prioritize user-friendly design for diverse user groups, including non-technical users.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0120.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0120\nCREATE TABLE `seasons` (\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_zero_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `regional_designation` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `regular_season_compact_results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_compact_results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_compact_results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winning_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_compact_results_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`losing_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `regular_season_detailed_results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `game_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_detailed_results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_detailed_results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winning_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `regular_season_detailed_results_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`losing_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_compact_results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_compact_results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_compact_results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winning_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_compact_results_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`losing_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_detailed_results` (\n  `result_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `game_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`result_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_detailed_results_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_detailed_results_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winning_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_detailed_results_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`losing_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `target` (\n  `target_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `predictions` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `win_loss_record` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`target_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_seeds` (\n  `seed_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`seed_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_seeds_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_seeds_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_slots` (\n  `slot_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `slot` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `strong_seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weak_seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`slot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_slots_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season_id`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_slots_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`strong_seed`) REFERENCES `tourney_seeds` (`seed_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_slots_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`weak_seed`) REFERENCES `tourney_seeds` (`seed_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
